sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-07> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel-checked Lean 4 statement about a model: Under the same hypotheses there exists a size above which the power required for flight exceeds the power available; the size exists, its value is not supplied." ;
    dct:description "Under the same hypotheses there exists a size above which the power required for flight exceeds the power available; the size exists, its value is not supplied." ;
    dct:source "On Growth and Form (1917)" ;
    skos:notation "undefined" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Corollary of R5 and R6 (Thompson's "a bird as large as a man could not fly").** There is a size above which the power required exceeds the power available. The size exists; its value is not supplied. -/
theorem exists_size_limit {W S M P : ℝ → ℝ} {k₁ k₂ kM ρ Cmax LD f p : ℝ} (hW : CubeLaw W k₁)
    (hS : AreaLaw S k₂) (hM : CubeLaw M kM) (hP : MusclePowerLaw P M f p) (hρ : 0 < ρ) (hCmax : 0 < Cmax)
    (hLD : 0 < LD) : ∃ Ls : ℝ, 0 < Ls ∧ ∀ L, Ls < L → P L < powerRequired (W L) (vmin ρ Cmax (W L) (S L)) LD"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.MusclePowerLaw" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.exists_size_limit" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Only the existence of a size above which power required exceeds power available is proved, under R1, R2, constant ρ, C_L,max, L/D and the muscle premise. Its value needs f, p, L/D, ρ and C_L,max, which no proof supplies, so nothing here says the ostrich, the moa or a man-sized bird is past it. The declaration in delphi:leanDeclaration (Delphi.MusclePowerLaw) is a NAMED HYPOTHESIS this theorem takes as an argument, not a definition the law rests on: it is Thompson's muscle premise (power available proportional to muscle mass at a constant mass-specific power), which is contested and is never asserted here, so the premise must not be read as the law." ;
    skos:note "The claim as the source states it, which is NOT what the kernel checked: \"Ostrich and moa have passed the size at which muscular flight is possible\" (On Growth and Form, 1917). What was checked is the statement in dct:description, which is about a model." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Everything in thompson1917-ch02-06, and that the family extends to the size in question with unchanged proportions; The value of L* needs f, p, L/D, ρ and C_L,max; the proof supplies none, so nothing here places the ostrich, the moa or a man-sized bird above it. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-07> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-07> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-07> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-thompson1917-ch02-07> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.exists_size_limit with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean (320 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.exists_size_limit: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [size-limit-at-every-size] Statement changed from the EXISTENCE of a size above which power required exceeds power available to the claim that it holds at EVERY positive size. That is false for small L (power available wins there), so the proof must fail. Without this mutant the ch02-07 record had no mutation evidence at all. Rejected with 2 error(s): Scaling.lean:226:9: error: Invalid `⟨...⟩` notation: The expected type Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-07> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Everything in thompson1917-ch02-06, and that the family extends to the size in question with unchanged proportions; The value of L* needs f, p, L/D, ρ and C_L,max; the proof supplies none, so nothing here places the ostrich, the moa or a man-sized bird above it. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

